<setup>
  <function name="f">sin(x)</function>
  <function name="f1P">cos(x)</function>
  <function name="f2P">-sin(x)</function>
  <function name="f3P">-cos(x)</function>
  <function name="g">cos(x)</function>
  <function name="g1P">-sin(x)</function>
  <function name="g2P">-cos(x)</function>
  <function name="g3P">sin(x)</function>
  <function name="h">exp(x)</function>

  <selectFromSequence name = "num1" from = "27" to = "32" step = "1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name = "k" from = "51" to = "75" step = "1"/>
  <number name="j">$k+5</number>
</setup>

<p>
  Three of the most important functions in mathematics are <m>\sin(x)</m>, <m>\cos(x)</m>, and <m>e^x</m>.  The two trigonometric functions are useful in modeling periodic phenomena such as sound waves, and the natural exponential function finds many different applications related to growth and decay.  These functions each also have the property that they are <em>infinitely differentiable</em>; this means that we can take as many derivatives of each as we'd like.
</p>

<p>
  In Section 1.6, we learned about the <em>second</em> derivative of a function: <m>f''(x)=\frac{d}{dx}[f'(x)]</m>.  In the same way, we can talk about the third, fourth, or even <m>n^{\text{th}}</m> derivative of a function.  For instance, <m>f'''(x)=\frac{d}{dx}[f''(x)]</m>, and <m>f^{(4)}(x)=\frac{d}{dx}[f'''(x)]</m> (after the third derivative, rather than writing a long list of <q>primes</q>, we instead write <q>(<m>n</m>)</q> to represent the number of the derivative we seek).
</p>

<p>

  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Fill in the following blanks to state formulas for the first <m>5</m> derivatives of <m>h(x) = e^x</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
         <m>\hspace{.8em} h(x) = e^x</m>
         <m> \hspace{3.4em}   h'(x) = </m><mathInput name="hp"/>
         <m> \hspace{1.65em}  h''(x) = </m><mathInput name="hpp"/>
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>h'''(x) = </m><mathInput name="hppp"/>
        <m> \quad \, h^{(4)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="hp4"/>
        <m>\quad \ h^{(5)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="hp5"/>
      </p>
      <!-- <p>
       <m>h^{(6)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="hp6"/>
        <m>\quad h^{(7)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="hp7"/>
        <m>\quad h^{(8)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="hp8"/>
      </p> -->
      <answer><award><when matchPartial>$hp=$h and $hpp = $h and $hppp=$h and $hp4 = $h and $hp5=$h</when></award></answer>

        <!-- <tabular>
          <row>
            <cell>
              <m>h(x) = e^x</m>
            </cell>
            <cell>
              <m>h'(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
            <cell>
              <m>h''(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>
              <m>h'''(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
            <cell>
              <m>h^{(4)}(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
            <cell>
              <m>h^{(5)}(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>
              <m>h^{(6)}(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
            <cell>
              <m>h^{(7)}(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
            <cell>
              <m>h^{(8)}(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>   -->
      <p>
        In addition, <m>h^{($num1)}(x) = </m><answer><award>$h</award></answer>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Fill in the following blanks to state formulas for the first <m>8</m> derivatives of <m>f(x) = \sin(x)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
         <m>\hspace{.8em} f(x) = \sin(x)</m>
         <m> \hspace{2em}   f'(x) = </m><mathInput name="fp"/>
         <m> \hspace{1.65em}  f''(x) = </m><mathInput name="fpp"/>
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>f'''(x) = </m><mathInput name="fppp"/>
        <m> \quad \, f^{(4)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="fp4"/>
        <m>\quad \ f^{(5)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="fp5"/>
      </p>
      <p>
       <m>f^{(6)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="fp6"/>
        <m>\quad f^{(7)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="fp7"/>
        <m>\quad f^{(8)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="fp8"/>
      </p>
      <answer><award><when matchPartial>$fp=$f1P and $fpp = $f2P and $fppp=$f3P and $fp4 = $f and $fp5=$f1P and $fp6 = $f2P and $fp7=$f3P and $fp8 = $f</when></award></answer>
      <p>
        In addition, <m>f^{($k)}(x) = </m>
              <answer>
                <mathInput name="fderivak"/>
                  <award>
                    <when>(<mod>$k 4</mod> = 1 and $fderivak = $f1P) or (<mod>$k 4</mod> = 2 and $fderivak = $f2P) or (<mod>$k 4</mod> = 3 and $fderivak = $f3P) or (<mod>$k 4</mod> = 0 and $fderivak = $f)</when>
                  </award>
              </answer>

      </p>
<!--
      <p>
        Testing:  <m>k = $k</m>, <mod>$k 4</mod>
      </p>
-->
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Fill in the following blanks to state formulas for the first <m>8</m> derivatives of <m>g(x) = \cos(x)</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
         <m>\hspace{.8em} g(x) = \cos(x)</m>
         <m> \hspace{2em}   g'(x) = </m><mathInput name="gp"/>
         <m> \hspace{1.65em}  g''(x) = </m><mathInput name="gpp"/>
      </p>
      <p>
        <m>g'''(x) = </m><mathInput name="gppp"/>
        <m> \quad \, g^{(4)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="gp4"/>
        <m>\quad \ g^{(5)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="gp5"/>
      </p>
      <p>
       <m>g^{(6)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="gp6"/>
        <m>\quad g^{(7)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="gp7"/>
        <m>\quad g^{(8)}(x) = </m><mathInput name="gp8"/>
      </p>
      <answer><award><when matchPartial>$gp=$g1P and $gpp = $g2P and $gppp=$g3P and $gp4 = $g and $gp5=$g1P and $gp6 = $g2P and $gp7=$g3P and $gp8 = $g</when></award></answer>

      <p>
        In addition, <m>g^{($j)}(x) = </m>
              <answer>
                <mathInput name="gderivaj"/>
                  <award>
                    <when>
                      (<mod>$j 4</mod> = 1 and $gderivaj = $g1P) or
                      (<mod>$j 4</mod> = 2 and $gderivaj = $g2P) or
                      (<mod>$j 4</mod> = 3 and $gderivaj = $g3P) or
                      (<mod>$j 4</mod> = 0 and $gderivaj = $g)
                    </when>
                  </award>
              </answer>
      </p>

      <!--
      <p>
        Testing:  <m>j = $j</m>, <mod>$j 4</mod>, <m>g(x)=$g</m>, <m>g'(x)=$g1P</m>, <m>g''(x)=$g2P</m>, <m>g'''(x)=$g3P</m>, $gjderiv
      </p>
      -->

    </li>
  </ol>

</p>  